<section id="about" class="card">
<h2>About EASJ Inc.</h2>
<p>Education Accountability and Social Justice (EASJ Inc.) is an independent non-profit advocacy organization dedicated to promoting quality education, accountability, transparency, social justice, human rights, and good governance throughout Liberia.</p>
</section>

<section id="leadership" class="card">
<h2>Founder & Executive Director</h2>
<p><strong>Advocate Amen Saakollie Sheriff</strong> is a Liberian educator, school administrator, sociologist, and social-justice and human-rights advocate. He is the Founder, CEO &amp; Executive Director of EASJ Inc., with extensive experience in education, public administration, civic education, accountability advocacy, and community engagement.</p>
<p>He is pursuing a Master of Education (M.Ed.) in Educational Administration and Supervision at Cuttington University School of Graduate and Professional Studies. His professional and advocacy interests include education accountability, governance, human rights, teacher and worker concerns, civic participation, and institutional strengthening.</p>
</section>

<section id="programs" class="card">
<h2>Programs &amp; Advocacy Areas</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Education Accountability:</strong> promoting quality, equitable and accountable education and supporting education stakeholders.</li>
<li><strong>Good Governance &amp; Transparency:</strong> encouraging responsible public service, institutional accountability and ethical governance.</li>
<li><strong>Justice &amp; Human Rights:</strong> advancing dignity, fairness, due process and protection of fundamental rights.</li>
<li><strong>Social Justice &amp; Community Empowerment:</strong> amplifying legitimate community concerns and supporting inclusive participation.</li>
<li><strong>Research &amp; Public Education:</strong> documenting issues, conducting civic education and promoting evidence-based public discussion.</li>
<li><strong>Teacher, Worker &amp; Youth Advocacy:</strong> promoting fair treatment, professional dignity and constructive engagement on workplace and education concerns.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="mission" class="card">
<h2>Mission</h2>
<p>To promote accountability, advance justice, empower communities, protect human rights, strengthen institutions, and support quality education through advocacy, research, public education, monitoring, constructive engagement, and collaborative action.</p>
<h2>Vision</h2>
<p>A Liberia where justice, fairness, freedom, accountability, human dignity, quality education, and strong institutions are upheld for all.</p>
</section>

<section id="partnership" class="card">
<h2>Partnership & Collaboration</h2>
